INSERT INTO `quest_template` (`entry`,`Method`,`ZoneOrSort`,`MinLevel`,`QuestLevel`,`Type`,`QuestFlags`,
  `SpecialFlags`,`RequiredCondition`,`RewXP`,`RewOrReqMoney`,`RewMoneyMaxLevel`,
  `RewItemId1`,`RewItemCount1`,`ReqCreatureOrGOId1`,`ReqCreatureOrGOCount1`,
  `Title`,`Details`,`Objectives`,`ObjectiveText1`,`RequestItemsText`,`OfferRewardText`) VALUES
  (919980,2,-9100,1,1,0,320,2049,920112,0,0,0,919602,1,920020,3,'Three at the Table','Anyone can win a game, $N. A good player wins them when it counts.$B$BSit down this week and show me three. Beat whoever takes the seat across from you, and don''t count on the shuffle to do it for you. Luck might carry you through one. It will not carry you through three.','Win three games of Hearthstone.','Games won','Three, $N. Two good wins are still only two.','Three wins, and not one of them handed to you. Good.$B$BThat''s a fair week''s work at the table. Take this, and come back when you want another test.'),
  (919981,2,-9100,1,1,0,320,2049,920112,0,0,0,919602,1,920021,8,'Time at the Table','A win teaches you what worked. A loss teaches you why. Either is worth more than a deck sitting in a box, $N.$B$BSit down and play eight games this week. Win, lose or draw, I don''t mind, so long as you see each one through to the end.','Play eight games of Hearthstone to the end.','Games played','Eight, $N, and finished ones. Walking away halfway does not count.','Eight games, played out. You know your deck better than you did last week, whether you admit it or not.$B$BHere.'),
  (919982,2,-9100,1,1,0,320,2049,920112,0,0,0,919602,1,920022,40,'A Long Evening','The hasty die early, $N. Most games are won in the turns after the first bad draw.$B$BTake forty turns this week, across as many games as it takes. Slow down and think each one through.','Take forty turns in games of Hearthstone.','Turns taken','Not forty yet, $N. Keep playing, and keep thinking.','Forty turns and, I hope, a few good ideas. Patience is most of this game.$B$BTake this.'),
  (919983,2,-9100,1,1,0,320,2049,920112,0,0,0,919602,1,920023,20,'The Hero Within','Every hero carries a trick of their own, $N, and most players forget theirs somewhere between the first card and the last.$B$BUse your hero power twenty times this week. A small edge, used often, beats a great deal of luck.','Use your hero power twenty times.','Hero powers used','Twenty, $N. Count them if you have to.','Twenty times, and every time on purpose, I hope. A small edge, used often, wins more games than any single bomb.$B$BHere you are.'),
  (919984,2,-9100,1,1,0,320,2049,920112,0,0,0,919602,1,920024,40,'Fortune''s Hand','A deck is only a promise until you draw from it, $N.$B$BDraw forty cards this week, and see what the promise is worth.','Draw forty cards in games of Hearthstone.','Cards drawn','Forty cards. The deck will keep, $N. Your week will not.','Forty cards through your hands. Some good, some not. That is the draw.$B$BTake this for your trouble.'),
  (919986,2,-9100,1,1,0,320,2049,920112,0,0,0,919602,1,920025,60,'Clearing the Board','A table full of the enemy''s minions is a table lost, $N. Don''t let it get that far.$B$BDestroy sixty minions this week. How you do it, I leave to you.','Destroy sixty minions in games of Hearthstone.','Minions destroyed','Sixty, $N. The rest of them are still standing.','Sixty down. I trust the board is quieter now.$B$BThis one is earned.'),
  (919987,2,-9100,1,1,0,320,2049,920112,0,0,0,919602,1,920026,50,'Calling the Troops','Few things win a game as plainly as the army you put on the table, $N.$B$BPlay fifty minions this week. Every one of them needs a place and a purpose.','Play fifty minions in games of Hearthstone.','Minions played','Fifty, $N. The table has room for a few more.','Fifty on the table. That''s more of an army than most of the regulars bring.$B$BHere.'),
  (919988,2,-9100,1,1,0,320,2049,920112,0,0,0,919602,1,920027,40,'Spell After Spell','Steel is fine, $N, but half this game is words, gestures and a little nerve.$B$BPlay forty spells this week. Don''t bother counting the misfires.','Play forty spells in games of Hearthstone.','Spells played','Forty, $N. Plenty of incantations left unsaid.','Forty spells. A few of them even did what you meant. Well done.$B$BTake this.'),
  (919989,2,-9100,1,1,0,320,2049,920112,0,0,0,919602,1,920028,12,'A Call of the Wild','Claws, teeth and an honest appetite, $N. There is a reason beasts have a seat at every table.$B$BPlay twelve of them this week, from whatever your deck keeps for the wild.','Play twelve Beasts in games of Hearthstone.','Beasts played','Twelve, $N. The rest are still out in the wild.','Twelve beasts, and I hope you fed them. Fine work.$B$BHere you are.'),
  (920110,2,-9100,1,1,0,320,2049,920112,0,0,0,919602,1,920035,3,'The Way of the Druid','Every class has its own way of winning, $N, and most players know only a few of them well.$B$BThe druids ask the wild for their strength, and it never comes cheap.$B$BWin three games this week with a Druid deck.','Win three games of Hearthstone with a Druid deck.','Druid games won','Three wins with a Druid deck, $N. Not with any other.','Three wins with the Druid. You''ve learned something about how it wins. Keep it.$B$BTake this.'),
  (920111,2,-9100,1,1,0,320,2049,920112,0,0,0,919602,1,920036,3,'The Way of the Hunter','Every class has its own way of winning, $N, and most players know only a few of them well.$B$BA hunter''s patience is only worth something if the prey falls.$B$BWin three games this week with a Hunter deck.','Win three games of Hearthstone with a Hunter deck.','Hunter games won','Three wins with a Hunter deck, $N. Not with any other.','Three wins with the Hunter. You''ve learned something about how it wins. Keep it.$B$BTake this.'),
  (920112,2,-9100,1,1,0,320,2049,920112,0,0,0,919602,1,920037,3,'The Way of the Mage','Every class has its own way of winning, $N, and most players know only a few of them well.$B$BEvery mage believes one more spell will be enough. Prove it three times.$B$BWin three games this week with a Mage deck.','Win three games of Hearthstone with a Mage deck.','Mage games won','Three wins with a Mage deck, $N. Not with any other.','Three wins with the Mage. You''ve learned something about how it wins. Keep it.$B$BTake this.'),
  (920113,2,-9100,1,1,0,320,2049,920112,0,0,0,919602,1,920038,3,'The Way of the Paladin','Every class has its own way of winning, $N, and most players know only a few of them well.$B$BThe Light will not win a game for you. It only gives you the chance.$B$BWin three games this week with a Paladin deck.','Win three games of Hearthstone with a Paladin deck.','Paladin games won','Three wins with a Paladin deck, $N. Not with any other.','Three wins with the Paladin. You''ve learned something about how it wins. Keep it.$B$BTake this.'),
  (920114,2,-9100,1,1,0,320,2049,920112,0,0,0,919602,1,920039,3,'The Way of the Priest','Every class has its own way of winning, $N, and most players know only a few of them well.$B$BA priest wins by outlasting everyone, which takes more nerve than it sounds.$B$BWin three games this week with a Priest deck.','Win three games of Hearthstone with a Priest deck.','Priest games won','Three wins with a Priest deck, $N. Not with any other.','Three wins with the Priest. You''ve learned something about how it wins. Keep it.$B$BTake this.'),
  (920115,2,-9100,1,1,0,320,2049,920112,0,0,0,919602,1,920040,3,'The Way of the Rogue','Every class has its own way of winning, $N, and most players know only a few of them well.$B$BA rogue wins in the few turns nobody was watching.$B$BWin three games this week with a Rogue deck.','Win three games of Hearthstone with a Rogue deck.','Rogue games won','Three wins with a Rogue deck, $N. Not with any other.','Three wins with the Rogue. You''ve learned something about how it wins. Keep it.$B$BTake this.'),
  (920116,2,-9100,1,1,0,320,2049,920112,0,0,0,919602,1,920041,3,'The Way of the Shaman','Every class has its own way of winning, $N, and most players know only a few of them well.$B$BThe elements follow a shaman, but only one who reads them right.$B$BWin three games this week with a Shaman deck.','Win three games of Hearthstone with a Shaman deck.','Shaman games won','Three wins with a Shaman deck, $N. Not with any other.','Three wins with the Shaman. You''ve learned something about how it wins. Keep it.$B$BTake this.'),
  (920117,2,-9100,1,1,0,320,2049,920112,0,0,0,919602,1,920042,3,'The Way of the Warlock','Every class has its own way of winning, $N, and most players know only a few of them well.$B$BA warlock pays for every gift, and wins when the price was worth it.$B$BWin three games this week with a Warlock deck.','Win three games of Hearthstone with a Warlock deck.','Warlock games won','Three wins with a Warlock deck, $N. Not with any other.','Three wins with the Warlock. You''ve learned something about how it wins. Keep it.$B$BTake this.'),
  (920118,2,-9100,1,1,0,320,2049,920112,0,0,0,919602,1,920043,3,'The Way of the Warrior','Every class has its own way of winning, $N, and most players know only a few of them well.$B$BA warrior has no secrets, only a plan and the strength to carry it out.$B$BWin three games this week with a Warrior deck.','Win three games of Hearthstone with a Warrior deck.','Warrior games won','Three wins with a Warrior deck, $N. Not with any other.','Three wins with the Warrior. You''ve learned something about how it wins. Keep it.$B$BTake this.'),
  (919990,2,-9100,1,1,0,320,2049,920112,0,0,0,919602,1,920029,1,'The Stranger at the Table','Most of the regulars will tell you who they want to play, $N. A real opponent doesn''t get asked.$B$BFace an opponent you did not choose, at the hardest level, and beat them. Take whoever you are given.','Defeat a random Hard opponent.','Hard opponents defeated','Not yet, $N. Whoever it is, they will not get any easier.','Someone you did not pick, at the hardest level, and you won. That is the whole game, really.$B$BTake this.'),
  (919991,2,-9100,1,1,0,320,2049,920112,0,0,0,919602,1,920030,3,'Without Losing Stride','A single win is an accident, $N. Three in a row is a habit.$B$BWin three games in a row this week. A loss in between sends you back to the beginning, so keep your head.','Win three games of Hearthstone in a row.','Wins in a row','Not yet, $N. One loss and you start over.','Three in a row, and no stumble. You''ll be hard to sit across from.$B$BHere.'),
  (919992,2,-9100,1,1,0,320,2049,920112,0,0,0,919602,1,920031,20,'Where It Counts','Boards, minions and tricks are only roads to the other hero, $N.$B$BDeal two hundred damage to enemy heroes this week. How you get there is up to you, but it has to land on the hero.','Deal two hundred damage to enemy heroes.','Damage dealt (in tens)','Two hundred, $N. Your opponents still have plenty of life left.','Two hundred damage. Their heroes will remember it, if nobody else does.$B$BTake this.'),
  (919993,2,-9100,1,1,0,320,2049,920112,0,0,0,919602,1,920032,1,'Quick and Quiet','Winning slowly is no shame, $N. Winning fast is a statement.$B$BWin a game this week in eight of your own turns or fewer. Don''t give them time to think.','Win a game of Hearthstone in eight turns or fewer.','Quick wins','Not fast enough yet, $N. Cut out the wasted turns.','Eight turns or fewer. I barely had time to sit down. Well played.$B$BHere.'),
  (919994,2,-9100,1,1,0,320,2049,920112,0,0,0,919602,1,920033,6,'A Heavy Hand','The big cards are the ones the table remembers, $N, but only if you live long enough to play them.$B$BPlay six cards that cost seven mana or more this week. Survive long enough to afford them.','Play six cards that cost seven or more mana.','Heavy cards played','Six, $N. Each of them costs a lot.','Six heavy plays, and you lived to make every one. That takes some doing.$B$BHere you are.');
